WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.849 --> 00:00:11.959
Frogs' legs were eaten in Britain for 7,000
years before they were eaten in France.

00:00:11.959 --> 00:00:16.680
Oliver Cromwell was dug up and beheaded two
years after his death.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.510
The ancient Egyptian word for 'cat' was pronounced
'miaow'.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:27.070
94% of terrorist campaigns fail to achieve
a single one of their strategic goals.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.560
Crickets produce their iconic chirping by
rubbing their forewings together.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.609
The sound is then heard by the female via
ear-like structures on her front legs.

00:00:36.609 --> 00:00:41.690
95% of the spiders in your house have never
been outside.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:47.120
The daddy-long-legs flosses after meals by
pulling each of its eight legs through its

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.120
jaws.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:53.989
The most difficult tongue-twister in English
is 'pad kid poured curd pulled cod'.

00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:58.710
The body of the sea otter has a pouch across
the front where it keeps rocks to break open

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.100
shellfish.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.370
The lawnmower is the most dangerous item in
the garden.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:06.360
The second most dangerous is the flowerpot.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.159
Eels can live inside sharks' hearts.

00:01:09.159 --> 00:01:16.479
In Japan, the number 42 is considered to be
unlucky, because four and two are pronounced

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:21.140
as shi and ni respectively, which can be translated
“to death”.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:28.420
The kite as we know it today was first invented
in China between 468 and 376 BC.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.880
The largest known star in the universe is
VY Canis Majoris.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:40.450
It sits nearly 5,000 light years from Earth
and is more than 1,540 times larger than our

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.450
Sun.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:48.149
If the rest of the planet's fresh water disappeared,
there would be enough left in Lake Baikal

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:52.420
to supply humanity for 50 years.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:57.750
The three Russian cosmonauts whose spacecraft
depressurised just before re-entry in 1971

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:13.909
are the only human beings to have died outside
the Earth's atmosphere.

